cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the ALICE benchmark, please cite the paper below."
title: "ALICE: A Large-Scale German Benchmark for Rubric-Based Multi-Dimensional Automatic Short Answer Scoring"
abstract: >-
  ALICE is a German short-answer scoring benchmark for K-12 STEM education
  (biology, chemistry, mathematics, physics). Every question carries its own
  rubric set across three scoring dimensions — learning performance, knowledge
  elements and skills — so that label semantics are represented as text rather
  than as a fixed classification head. Two test splits separate generalisation
  to unseen answers from generalisation to unseen questions.
type: dataset
